 # Recording story save native checks
 
 `node experiments/pg17-recording-flow/verify.mjs --without-migration` demonstrates missing-RPC RED. Run without arguments for isolated PostgreSQL 17.4 reservation, terminal confirmation, permissions and concurrent deletion checks. `fixture.mjs` exports `setup`, `fresh`, `save`, and synthetic constants for subsequent browser integration. The story table uses the exact bootstrap CREATE TABLE; other platform prerequisites remain synthetic. No remote service, cloud Storage, paid model, family data or G1 device qualification is involved.
+
+`node experiments/pg17-recording-flow/verify.mjs --before-final-fix` runs the current tests and actual compiled application confirmation service against the SQL frozen in `.superpowers/sdd/2026-11-05-upgrade-g1-recording-flow/final-fix-before/`. It reproduces the final-review I1 committed-story/API-rejection defect. This option is separate from `--before-fix-1`, which reproduces the earlier immutable-identity defect; historical SQL options are mutually exclusive. Each run writes a unique `native-.../results.json` under `docs/research/evidence/2026-11-05-g1-recording-flow/` and leaves previous evidence intact.
+
+`confirmation-regressions.mjs` checks each historical worker/provider/request/usage/cost field in real two- and three-attempt chains, exact numbering, chronological history, and successful-chain timestamp domains. `fresh(..., true, { attemptCount: 2 | 3 })` uses actual 1000 ms lease claims, PostgreSQL-clock expiry, recovery, latest dispatch, candidate reservation/preparation and publication routines. It never constructs successful attempt history by inserting rows or rewriting deadlines. All unmodified corruption controls first pass the real application's lookup validator. Valid two-/three-attempt confirmations and replay are checked through the actual service, as is an early-AD UTC timestamp control from an Asia/Taipei SQL connection.
+
+The report records complete baseline/corrupted snapshots, lease transitions, service outcomes, and full PostgreSQL JSON story/intent rows before and after confirmation. It collects every corruption outcome before asserting, so RED records all affected fields. Failed confirmation must return no cleanup receipt and leave both complete rows equal; GREEN must reject with 409 from SQL before DML. Existing canonical-identity, publication-corruption, permission and lock-wait cases remain in the runner.
+
+Native schema constraints stay enabled: zero/negative or duplicate attempt numbers are already forbidden, and candidate timestamps cannot be infinite or reverse preparation order. Candidate BC/five-digit-year checks therefore mutate a finite ordered timestamp pair. The fixture's Storage metadata and auth/project prerequisites remain synthetic; RPC transport is a local adapter backed by an actual unprivileged PostgreSQL service-role connection. These tests establish local SQL/application consistency, not hosted Supabase, real audio decoding, the complete deployed migration chain, or G1 qualification.
